        "# Capstone 85 \u2014 Content Classifier Integration Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/classifiers.py` defines all three classifiers. Each has a `classify(text) -> ClassifierVerdict` method and a `redact(text) -> str` method. `code/main.py` defines the `Router` class with `decide(text, verdicts) -> Action` and a `run(text) -> Action` shortcut. The demo wires the three classifiers behind one router and runs a small corpus of crafted outputs that exercise each severity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Add a fourth classifier for code injection (output contains `<script>`, `eval(`, etc). Decide its severity policy and integrate it.\n2. Make the router apply a per-classifier severity weight so PII counts more than toxicity. Demonstrate the change on the same fixtures.\n3. Add a confidence threshold so low-score verdicts downgrade by one severity level. Sweep the threshold and report how block rate changes."
      ]
    }
  ],
